econnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\"/><link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"/><link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://www.googletagmanager.com\"/><link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://www.google-analytics.com\"/><link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://analytics.ahrefs.com\"/><link rel=\"dns-prefetch\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\"/><link rel=\"dns-prefetch\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\"/><link rel=\"dns-prefetch\" href=\"https://www.googletagmanager.com\"/><link rel=\"dns-prefetch\" href=\"https://www.google-analytics.com\"/><link rel=\"dns-prefetch\" href=\"https://analytics.ahrefs.com\"/><link rel=\"dns-prefetch\" href=\"https://www.irs.gov\"/><link rel=\"dns-prefetch\" href=\"https://taxfoundation.org\"/><link rel=\"manifest\" href=\"/manifest.json\"/><meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#0a0f1e\"/><meta name=\"next-size-adjust\" content=\"\"/><title>2026 State Tax Burden Analysis: All 50 States Ranked | TheTaxCalc Research | TheTaxCalc</title><meta name=\"description\" content=\"Original 2026 cross-sectional study comparing effective state and local tax burdens across all 50 U.S. states. Findings, methodology, and interactive data for four household income profiles.\"/><meta name=\"author\" content=\"Rachel Mitchell, CPA\"/><meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"state tax burden 2026,state tax comparison,effective tax rate by state,state income tax rankings,tax burden study,state and local taxes,best states for taxes,worst states for taxes\"/><meta name=\"creator\" content=\"TheTaxCalc\"/><meta name=\"publisher\" content=\"TheTaxCalc\"/><meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow\"/><meta name=\"googlebot\" content=\"index, follow, max-video-preview:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1\"/><meta name=\"category\" content=\"finance\"/><meta name=\"classification\" content=\"Tax Calculator\"/><link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://thetaxcalc.com/research/2026-state-tax-burden\"/><meta name=\"google-site-verification\" content=\"7bdac16b5ecbdd40\"/><meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"2026 State Tax Burden Analysis: All 50 States Ranked\"/><meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Original research ranking all 50 U.S. states by effective tax burden for 2026. Four household income profiles.\"/><meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://thetaxcalc.com/research/2026-state-tax-burden\"/><meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"TheTaxCalc\"/><meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\"/><meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\"/><meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\"/><meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"TheTaxCalc — Free 2026 Paycheck &amp; Mortgage Calculator\"/><meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Compute your take-home pay after federal, FICA, and state taxes. Supports IL, TX, FL, CA, NY.\"/><meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://thetaxcalc.com/opengraph-image.png\"/><link rel=\"icon\" href=\"/favicon.ico\"/><link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" href=\"/apple-touch-icon.png\"/><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/#organization\",\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\",\"logo\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/icon.png\"},\"description\":\"Free 2026 tax calculators — paycheck, mortgage, 401(k), capital gains, and self-employment. Trusted by thousands of users for accurate, up-to-date tax estimates.\",\"foundingDate\":\"2022\",\"sameAs\":[\"https://thetaxcalc.com/about\",\"https://thetaxcalc.com/blog\",\"https://thetaxcalc.com/research\",\"https://thetaxcalc.com/methodology\"],\"contactPoint\":[{\"@type\":\"ContactPoint\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/about#contact\",\"contactType\":\"customer support\",\"availableLanguage\":[\"English\"]}]},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/#website\",\"@type\":\"WebSite\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\",\"description\":\"Free 2026 tax calculators — paycheck, mortgage, 401(k), capital gains, and self-employment.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/#organization\"},\"potentialAction\":{\"@type\":\"SearchAction\",\"target\":{\"@type\":\"EntryPoint\",\"urlTemplate\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/?q={search_term_string}\"},\"query-input\":\"required name=search_term_string\"}},{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/#webpage-home\",\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"name\":\"2026 Tax Calculator — Paycheck & Take-Home Pay | 50 States\",\"description\":\"Free 2026 tax calculator. Take-home pay after federal, FICA & state tax. 64 tools & 50-state sales tax data. No sign-up.\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/#website\"},\"about\":{\"@type\":\"Thing\",\"name\":\"Tax Calculator\"}}]}</script><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/0cz1d0mv5g_q7.js\" noModule=\"\"></script></head><body class=\"geist_a71539c9-module__T19VSG__variable geist_mono_8d43a2aa-module__8Li5zG__variable antialiased bg-background text-foreground\"><div hidden=\"\"><!--$--><!--/$--></div><a href=\"#main-content\" class=\"sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:fixed focus:top-4 focus:left-4 focus:z-[9999] focus:rounded-lg focus:bg-emerald-600 focus:px-4 focus:py-2 focus:text-white focus:shadow-lg\">Skip to main content</a><div class=\"min-h-screen flex flex-col bg-background bg-mesh\"><a href=\"#main-content\" class=\"sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:fixed focus:top-4 focus:left-4 focus:z-[100] focus:rounded-lg focus:bg-emerald-600 focus:px-4 focus:py-2 focus:text-white focus:shadow-lg\">Skip to main content</a><header class=\"sticky top-0 z-[100] w-full glass-strong overflow-visible\"><div class=\"h-[2px] bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-emerald-500/60 to-transparent\"></div><div class=\"mx-auto flex h-16 max-w-7xl items-center justify-between px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 overflow-visible\"><a class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 transition-all hover:opacity-90 group\" href=\"/\"><div class=\"relative flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-500 to-emerald-600 shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/20 group-hover:shadow-emerald-500/30 transition-shadow\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-dollar-sign h-5 w-5 text-white\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><line x1=\"12\" x2=\"12\" y1=\"2\" y2=\"22\"></line><path d=\"M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6\"></path></svg><div class=\"absolute inset-0 rounded-xl bg-white/10 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity\"></div></div><span class=\"text-lg font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground\">TheTaxCalc<span class=\"gradient-text\">.com</span></span></a><nav class=\"hidden items-center gap-1 lg:flex\"><div class=\"relative\" style=\"z-index:110\"><button class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-calculator h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"16\" height=\"20\" x=\"4\" y=\"2\" rx=\"2\"></rect><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"16\" y1=\"6\" y2=\"6\"></line><line x1=\"16\" x2=\"16\" y1=\"14\" y2=\"18\"></line><path d=\"M16 10h.01\"></path><path d=\"M12 10h.01\"></path><path d=\"M8 10h.01\"></path><path d=\"M12 14h.01\"></path><path d=\"M8 14h.01\"></path><path d=\"M12 18h.01\"></path><path d=\"M8 18h.01\"></path></svg>Calculators<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down h-3 w-3 transition-transform\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></button></div><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/compare\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right-left h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m16 3 4 4-4 4\"></path><path d=\"M20 7H4\"></path><path d=\"m8 21-4-4 4-4\"></path><path d=\"M4 17h16\"></path></svg>Compare</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/glossary\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-book-open h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M12 7v14\"></path><path d=\"M3 18a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5a4 4 0 0 1 4 4 4 4 0 0 1 4-4h5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-6a3 3 0 0 0-3 3 3 3 0 0 0-3-3z\"></path></svg>Glossary</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/blog\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-book-open h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M12 7v14\"></path><path d=\"M3 18a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5a4 4 0 0 1 4 4 4 4 0 0 1 4-4h5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-6a3 3 0 0 0-3 3 3 3 0 0 0-3-3z\"></path></svg>Blog</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/salary\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-trending-up h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M16 7h6v6\"></path><path d=\"m22 7-8.5 8.5-5-5L2 17\"></path></svg>Salary</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/tax-data\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chart-column h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg>Data</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/widgets\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-code-xml h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m18 16 4-4-4-4\"></path><path d=\"m6 8-4 4 4 4\"></path><path d=\"m14.5 4-5 16\"></path></svg>Widgets</a></nav><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><a class=\"hidden sm:flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-600 to-emerald-500 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/20 hover:shadow-emerald-500/30 transition-all hover:scale-[1.02]\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chart-column h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg>Calculate Now</a><button data-slot=\"button\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium transition-all disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 shrink-0 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive hover:bg-accent dark:hover:bg-accent/50 h-8 rounded-md gap-1.5 px-3 has-[&gt;svg]:px-2.5 lg:hidden text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground\" aria-label=\"Toggle mobile menu\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-menu h-5 w-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 12h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 18h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 6h16\"></path></svg></button></div></div></header><main id=\"main-content\" class=\"flex-1\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"ScholarlyArticle\",\"headline\":\"Comparative Analysis of State Tax Burdens Across the 50 United States: A 2026 Cross-Sectional Study\",\"author\":[{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Rachel Mitchell\",\"jobTitle\":\"CPA, Lead Researcher\",\"affiliation\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc Research Division\"}},{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"David Chen\",\"jobTitle\":\"Data Analyst\",\"affiliation\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc Research Division\"}}],\"datePublished\":\"2026-07-04\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-07-04\",\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},\"about\":[\"State taxation\",\"Tax burden\",\"Public finance\",\"United States\"],\"abstract\":\"This study presents a comparative cross-sectional analysis of state and local tax burdens across all 50 U.S. states for the 2026 tax year. Using a standardized methodology integrating state income tax schedules, sales tax rates, property tax assessments, and excise taxes, we compute effective total tax burdens for representative household profiles at four income levels: $35,000, $75,000, $150,000, and $300,000.\",\"keywords\":\"state income tax, tax burden, effective tax rate, tax policy, comparative analysis, United States\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/research/2026-state-tax-burden\",\"citation\":[{\"@type\":\"CreativeWork\",\"name\":\"State and Local Tax Burden Rankings: 2026 Update\",\"publisher\":\"Tax Foundation\"},{\"@type\":\"CreativeWork\",\"name\":\"American Community Survey 5-Year Estimates\",\"publisher\":\"U.S. Census Bureau\"}]}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Dataset\",\"name\":\"2026 State Tax Burden Data: 50 States, 4 Income Profiles\",\"description\":\"Effective total state and local tax burden percentages for all 50 U.S. states, computed for four representative household profiles ($35K, $75K, $150K, $300K) for the 2026 tax year.\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/research/2026-state-tax-burden\",\"creator\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc Research Division\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},\"datePublished\":\"2026-07-04\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-07-04\",\"keywords\":\"state tax, tax burden, effective rate, 2026, United States\",\"distribution\":[{\"@type\":\"DataDownload\",\"encodingFormat\":\"text/html\",\"contentUrl\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/research/2026-state-tax-burden\"}],\"variableMeasured\":[{\"@type\":\"PropertyValue\",\"name\":\"State\",\"valueText\":\"U.S. state\"},{\"@type\":\"PropertyValue\",\"name\":\"Income Tax\",\"valueText\":\"Effective state income tax rate\"},{\"@type\":\"PropertyValue\",\"name\":\"Sales Tax\",\"valueText\":\"Effective sales tax burden\"},{\"@type\":\"PropertyValue\",\"name\":\"Property Tax\",\"valueText\":\"Effective property tax rate\"},{\"@type\":\"PropertyValue\",\"name\":\"Total Burden\",\"valueText\":\"Total effective state and local tax burden percentage\"}],\"license\":\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\",\"isAccessibleForFree\":true}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Research\",\"item\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/research\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"2026 State Tax Burden\",\"item\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/research/2026-state-tax-burden\"}]}</script><article class=\"mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\"><nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"mb-6 flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><a class=\"hover:text-foreground transition-colors\" href=\"/\">Home</a><span aria-hidden=\"true\">/</span><a class=\"hover:text-foreground transition-colors\" href=\"/research\">Research</a><span aria-hidden=\"true\">/</span><span class=\"text-foreground font-medium\">2026 State Tax Burden</span></nav><header class=\"mb-10\"><div class=\"mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/10 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-emerald-400\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-file-text h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M15 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7Z\"></path><path d=\"M14 2v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h4\"></path><path d=\"M10 9H8\"></path><path d=\"M16 13H8\"></path><path d=\"M16 17H8\"></path></svg>Original Research Study</div><h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl mb-4\">Comparative Analysis of State Tax Burdens Across the 50 United States: A 2026 Cross-Sectional Study</h1><div class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><span>By Rachel Mitchell, CPA &amp; David Chen</span><span>•</span><span>Published July 4, 2026</span><span>•</span><span>12 min read</span></div></header><section class=\"mb-10 rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/30 p-6\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3\">Abstract</h2><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-3\">This study presents a comparative cross-sectional analysis of state and local tax burdens across all 50 U.S. states for the 2026 tax year. Using a standardized methodology that integrates state income tax schedules, state-level sales tax rates, property tax assessments, and excise taxes, we compute effective total tax burdens for representative household profiles at four income levels: $35,000, $75,000, $150,000, and $300,000.</p><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><strong>Keywords:</strong> state income tax, tax burden, effective tax rate, tax policy, comparative analysis, United States, public finance.</p></section><section class=\"mb-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">Key Findings</h2><div class=\"space-y-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3 rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 p-4\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chart-column mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 flex-shrink-0 text-emerald-400\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg><div><p class=\"font-semibold text-foreground\">Wide variation in effective burdens</p><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Total effective state tax burdens range from <strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">0.0% in Alaska</strong> to<!-- --> <strong class=\"text-rose-400\">13.3% in California</strong> for the $150,000 married household profile — a gap of over 13 percentage points.</p></div></div><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3 rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/30 p-4\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-trending-down mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 flex-shrink-0 text-emerald-400\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M16 17h6v-6\"></path><path d=\"m22 17-8.5-8.5-5 5L2 7\"></path></svg><div><p class=\"font-semibold text-foreground\">Tax burden correlates with outmigration</p><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Regression analysis shows a significant negative correlation (r = -0.42, p &lt; 0.01) between state tax burden and net domestic migration over 2021-2025, suggesting tax differentials influence household relocation decisions.</p></div></div><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3 rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/30 p-4\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-file-text mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 flex-shrink-0 text-emerald-400\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M15 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7Z\"></path><path d=\"M14 2v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h4\"></path><path d=\"M10 9H8\"></path><path d=\"M16 13H8\"></path><path d=\"M16 17H8\"></path></svg><div><p class=\"font-semibold text-foreground\">Seven states have no income tax</p><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Alaska, Florida, Nevada, South Dakota, Texas, Washington, and Wyoming impose no broad-based individual income tax. New Hampshire taxes only dividend and interest income (phased out completely in 2025).</p></div></div></div></section><section class=\"mb-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">Methodology Summary</h2><p class=\"text-muted-foreground mb-4\">We model four components of state and local taxation: (1) state individual income tax using each state&#x27;s 2026 brackets, deductions, and exemptions; (2) state-level sales tax applied to a representative consumption basket; (3) property tax at median effective rates applied to median-valued owner-occupied housing; and (4) excise taxes on gasoline at average annual consumption.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground\">Four representative household profiles are used: P1 ($35K single renter), P2 ($75K married with 2 children, $250K home), P3 ($150K married with 2 children, $400K home), and P4 ($300K married with 2 children, $700K home). The table below shows results for Profile P3. See the full methodology page for details on all profiles.</p></section><section class=\"mb-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">2026 Effective State Tax Burden Rankings</h2><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4\">Profile P3: $150,000 married household with 2 children, $400,000 home.</p><div class=\"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border/30\"><table class=\"w-full text-sm\"><thead class=\"bg-card/50\"><tr><th class=\"px-3 py-2 text-left font-semibold text-foreground\">Rank</th><th class=\"px-3 py-2 text-left font-semibold text-foreground\">State</th><th class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-semibold text-foreground\">Income Tax</th><th class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-semibold text-foreground\">Sales Tax</th><th class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-semibold text-foreground\">Property Tax</th><th class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-semibold text-emerald-400\">Total</th></tr></thead><tbody class=\"divide-y divide-border/20\"><tr class=\"bg-emerald-500/5\"><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-muted-foreground\">1</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 font-medium text-foreground\">Alaska</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\">0.0<!-- -->%</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\">1.76<!-- -->%</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\">1.18<!-- -->%</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-bold text-emerald-400\">4.6<!-- -->%</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-emerald-500/5\"><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-muted-foreground\">2</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 font-medium text-foreground\">Wyoming</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\">0.0<!-- -->%</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\">4.00<!-- -->%</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\">0.61<!-- -->%</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-bold text-emerald-400\">5.8<!-- -->%</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-emerald-500/5\"><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-muted-foreground\">3</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 font-medium text-foreground\">Florida</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\">0.0<!-- -->%</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\">6.00<!-- -->%</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\">0.83<!-- -->%</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-bold text-emerald-400\">6.2<!-- -->%</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-emerald-500/5\"><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-muted-foreground\">4</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 font-medium text-foreground\">Tennessee</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\">0.0<!-- -->%</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\">7.00<!-- -->%</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\">0.71<!-- -->%</td><td class=\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-bold t