font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl mb-4\",\"children\":\"Comparative Analysis of State Tax Burdens Across the 50 United States: A 2026 Cross-Sectional Study\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"By Rachel Mitchell, CPA & David Chen\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"•\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Published July 4, 2026\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"•\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"12 min read\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10 rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/30 p-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3\",\"children\":\"Abstract\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-3\",\"children\":\"This study presents a comparative cross-sectional analysis of state and local tax burdens across all 50 U.S. states for the 2026 tax year. Using a standardized methodology that integrates state income tax schedules, state-level sales tax rates, property tax assessments, and excise taxes, we compute effective total tax burdens for representative household profiles at four income levels: $35,000, $75,000, $150,000, and $300,000.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Keywords:\"}],\" state income tax, tax burden, effective tax rate, tax policy, comparative analysis, United States, public finance.\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Key Findings\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-3 rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 p-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$unde