.5-5 5L2 7\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Tax burden correlates with outmigration\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Regression analysis shows a significant negative correlation (r = -0.42, p < 0.01) between state tax burden and net domestic migration over 2021-2025, suggesting tax differentials influence household relocation decisions.\"}]]}]]}]\n30:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-3 rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/30 p-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-file-text mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 flex-shrink-0 text-emerald-400\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"1rqfz7\",{\"d\":\"M15 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7Z\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"tnqrlb\",{\"d\":\"M14 2v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h4\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"b1mrlr\",{\"d\":\"M10 9H8\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"t4e002\",{\"d\":\"M16 13H8\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"z1uh3a\",{\"d\":\"M16 17H8\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Seven states have no income tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Alaska, Florida, Nevada, South Dakota, Texas, Washington, and Wyoming impose no broad-based individual income tax. New Hampshire taxes only dividend and interest income (phased out completely in 2025).\"}]]}]]}]\n31:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Methodology Summary\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"We model four components of state and local taxation: (1) state individual income tax using each state's 2026 brackets, deductions, and exemptions; (2) state-level sales tax applied to a representative consumption basket; (3) property tax at median effective rates applied to median-valued owner-occupied housing; and (4) excise taxes on gasoline at average annual consumption.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Four representative household profiles are used: P1 ($35K single renter), P2 ($75K married with 2 children, $250K home), P3 ($150K married with 2 children, $400K home), and P4 ($300K married with 2 children, $700K home). The table below shows results for Profile P3. See the full methodology page for details on all profiles.\"}]]}]\n32:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"2026 Effective State Tax Burden Rankings\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Profile P3: $150,000 married household with 2 children, $400,000 home.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border/30\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"table\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"thead\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-card/50\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-left font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Rank\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-left font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"State\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Income Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Sales Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Property Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-semibold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"Total\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"tbody\",null,{\"className\":\"divide-y divide-border/20\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"tr\",\"Alaska\",{\"className\":\"bg-emerald-500/5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":1}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Alaska\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"0.0\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"1.76\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"1.18\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-bold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":[\"4.6\",\"%\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",\"Wyoming\",{\"className\":\"bg-emerald-500/5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":2}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Wyoming\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"0.0\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"4.00\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"0.61\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-bold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":[\"5.8\",\"%\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",\"Florida\",{\"className\":\"bg-emerald-500/5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":3}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Florida\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"0.0\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"6.00\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"0.83\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-bold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":[\"6.2\",\"%\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",\"Tennessee\",{\"className\":\"bg-emerald-500/5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":4}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Tennessee\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"0.0\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"7.00\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"0.71\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right font-bold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":[\"6.4\",\"%\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",\"South Dakota\",{\"className\":\"bg-emerald-500/5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":5}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"South Dakota\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"0.0\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"4.50\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-3 py-2 text-right text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"1.32\",\"%\"]}],\"$L39\"]}],\"$L3a\",\"$L3b\",\"$L3c\",\"$L3d\",\"$L3e\",\"$L3f\",\"$L40\",\"$L41\",\"$L42\",\"$L43\",\"$L44\",\"$L45\",\"$L46\",\"$L47\",\"$L48\",\"$L49\",\"$L4a\",\"$L4b\",\"$L4c\",\"$L4d\",\"$L4e\",\"$L4f\",\"$L50\",\"$L51\",\"$L52\",\"$L53\",\"$L54\",\"$L55\",\"$L56\",\"$L57\",\"$L58\",\"$L59\",\"$L5a\",\"$L5b\",\"$L5c\",\"$L5d\",\"$L5e\",\"$L5f\",\"$L60\",\"$L61\",\"$L62\",\"$L63\",\"$L64\",\"$L65\",\"$L66\"]}]]}]}],\"$L67\"]}]\n33:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Discussion & Implications\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-4 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"The substantial variation in effective state tax burdens documented in this study has important implications for household financial planning, employer compensation design, and state tax policy. For households with location flexibility — particularly remote workers and retirees — the cumulative effect of state tax differentials can exceed $20,000 annually for the P3 income profile, representing a meaningful share of disposable income.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"For policymakers, the negative correlation between tax burden and net migration raises questions about the long-run revenue implications of high-tax regimes. While our analysis cannot establish causation, the consistent pattern across multiple income profiles and time periods suggests tax differentials are a meaningful factor in household location decisions, particularly among high-income households.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"The recent trend toward flat tax structures — adopted by 14 states as of 2026, up from 8 in 2020 — reflects a deliberate policy choice to simplify administration and reduce marginal rate effects. Our data show flat-tax states have, on average, lower effective burdens across all four income profiles.\"}]]}]]}]\n34:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Limitations\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Several limitations should be noted. Our representative household profiles simplify real household heterogeneity. Actual tax burdens vary based on specific deductions, credits, and circumstances. Our consumption basket reflects national averages. Property tax assessments use median values; actual burdens depend on local practices. Migration analysis is correlational and cannot establish causation — multiple confounding factors including housing costs, climate, and labor market conditions also influence migration decisions.\"}]]}]\n35:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"References\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"Tax Foundation. (2026). \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"State and Local Tax Burden Rankings: 2026 Update\"}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"U.S. Census Bureau. (2025). \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"American Community Survey 5-Year Estimates\"}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"Bureau of Labor Statistics. (2025). \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"Consumer Expenditure Survey: 2024 Annual Report\"}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"Internal Revenue Service. (2026). \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"Publication 15 (Circular E): Employer's Tax Guide\"}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"McLure, C. E. (2024). State tax policy in the post-pandemic era. \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"National Tax Journal\"}],\", 77(2), 145-172.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"Gale, W. G., Krupkin, A., & Rueben, K. (2025). State tax reform options for 2026. \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"Tax Policy Center Report\"}],\".\"]}]]}]]}]\n36:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-emerald-500/30 bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-500/5 to-emerald-500