ng a standardized methodology that integrates state income tax schedules, state-level sales tax rates, property tax assessments, and excise taxes, we compute effective total tax burdens for representative household profiles at four income levels: $35,000, $75,000, $150,000, and $300,000.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Keywords:\"}],\" state income tax, tax burden, effective tax rate, tax policy, comparative analysis, United States, public finance.\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Key Findings\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-3 rounded-lg border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 p-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-chart-column mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 flex-shrink-0 text-emerald-400\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"c24i48\",{\"d\":\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"2bz60n\",{\"d\":\"M18 17V9\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"1frdt8\",{\"d\":\"M13 17V5\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"17ska0\",{\"d\":\"M8 17v-3\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Wide variation in effective burdens\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"Total effective state tax burdens range from \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"0.0% in Alaska\"}],\" to\",\" \",\"$L2e\",\" for the $150,000 married household profile — a gap of over 13 percentage points.\"]}]]}]]}],\"$L2f\",\"$L30\"]}]]}],\"$L31\",\"$L32\",\"$L33\",\"$L34\",\"$L35\",\"$L36\"]}]\n26:[\"$\",\"$L37\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$2b\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@38\"}]}]\n2e:[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-rose-400\",\"children\":\"13.3% in California\"}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-3 rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/30 p-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-trending-down mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 flex-shrink-0 text-emerald-400\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"t6n2it\",{\"d\":\"M16 17h6v-6\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"x473p\",{\"d\":\"m22 17-8.5-8.5-5 5L2 7\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Tax burden correlates with outmigration\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Regression analysis shows a significant negative correlation (r = -0.42, p < 0.01) between state tax burden and net domestic migration over 2021-2025, suggesting tax differentials influence household relocation decisions.\"}]]}]]}]\n30:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-3 rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/30 p-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-file-text mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 flex-shrink-0 text-emerald-400\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"1rqfz7\",{\"d\":\"M15 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7Z\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"tnqrlb\",{\"d\":\"M14 2v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h4\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"b1mrlr\",{\"d\":\"M10 9H8\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"t4e002\",{\"d\":\"M16 13H8\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"z1uh3a\",{\"d\":\"M16 17H8\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Seven states have no income tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Alaska, Florida, Nevada, South Dakota, Texas, Washington, and Wyoming impose no broad-based individual income tax. New Hampshire taxes only dividend and interest income (phased out completely in 2025).\"}]]}]]}]\n31:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Methodology Summary\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"We model four components of state and local taxation: (1) state individual income tax using each state's 2026 brackets, deductions, and exemptions; (2) state-level sales tax applied to a representative consumption basket; (3) property tax at median effective rates applied to median-valued owner-occupied housing; and (4) excise taxes on gasoline at average annual consumption.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Four representative household profiles are used: P1 ($35K single renter), P2 ($75K married with 2 children, $250K home), P3 ($150K married with 2 children, $400K home), and P4 ($300K married with 2 children, $700K home). The table below shows results for Profile P3. See the full methodology page for details on all profiles.\"}]]}]\n32:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"2026 Effective State Tax Bur